---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';import {evidence,articles,publication,url} from '../../lib/content';
export function getStaticPaths(){return evidence.map(record=>({params:{id:record.id},props:{record}}))}
const {record}=Astro.props;const backlinks=articles.filter(a=>a.evidence.includes(record.id));
---
<Base title={`${record.id}: ${record.title}`} description={record.observation}><div class="article-topline"><a href={url('evidence/')}>← Evidence ledger</a><span>{record.id} / REPORTED OBSERVATION</span></div><header class="article-heading evidence-heading"><div class="evidence-label"><i class="line"/>{record.environment}</div><h1>{record.title}</h1><p>{record.observation}</p></header><div class="evidence-layout"><aside><dl class="record-facts"><dt>Record</dt><dd>{record.id}</dd><dt>Environment</dt><dd>{record.environment}</dd><dt>Editorial review</dt><dd>{record.reviewedOn}</dd><dt>Method</dt><dd>{record.method}</dd><dt>Reviewed snapshot</dt><dd><code>{publication.sourceRevision.slice(0,7)}</code></dd><dt>Public reproducibility</dt><dd>Summary and provenance only</dd></dl></aside><div><section class="record-limit"><span class="section-number">THE BOUNDARY OF THE CLAIM</span><h2>What this does not establish</h2><p>{record.limits}</p></section>{record.measurements.length>0&&<section class="measurements"><h2>Recorded values</h2><dl>{record.measurements.map(m=><div><dt>{m.label}</dt><dd class:list={{untested:/not tested|not established|unmeasured/i.test(m.value)}}>{m.value}</dd></div>)}</dl><p>Values are transcribed into this curated record. Their experimental scope is described above.</p></section>}<section class="record-provenance"><h2>Provenance</h2><p>The following private project documents support this editorial record. Their hashes preserve the identity of the reviewed versions. The documents, firmware and raw run artifacts are not included in this publication.</p>{record.records.map(r=><details><summary>{r.document}</summary><dl><dt>SHA-256 of reviewed document</dt><dd><code class="long-hash">{r.sha256}</code></dd><dt>Access</dt><dd>{r.access}</dd></dl></details>)}<a class="text-link" href={url('sources/#provenance')}>How evidence is reviewed and published →</a></section><section class="related"><h2>Used in these chapters</h2><div>{backlinks.map(a=><a href={url('articles/'+a.slug+'/')}><span>{a.section}</span><strong>{a.title}</strong><span>→</span></a>)}</div></section></div></div></Base>
